<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/033J">Proposition <span data-tag="033J">4.5.3.19</span> <span class="named">(Transitivity)</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a commutative diagram of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}' \ar [d] \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'' \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}' \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}'', } \]
</div>
<p> where the square on the right is a categorical pullback. Then the square on the left is a categorical pullback if and only if the outer rectangle is a categorical pullback. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Propositions <a data-tag="033C" href="/tag/033C">4.5.3.15</a> and <a data-tag="0110" href="/tag/0110">3.4.1.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
